blocks.text:
Lena buys a sandwich at a kiosk – part of the price goes to the state as tax. {{1}}
Mr Brunner declares his pay on his annual tax return and then receives his tax bill. {{2}}
A furniture manufacturer has earned two million CHF after deducting all costs and pays tax on this amount. {{3}}
A tax that was already included in the sale price appears on the receipt for a mobile phone. {{4}}
A doctor pays tax on her annual income. {{5}}
A start-up makes a profit for the first time – tax is now due on it. {{6}}
When you buy a cinema ticket, you pay the tax without noticing – it is included in the price. {{7}}
Ms Meier gets a pay rise – her annual tax bill increases as a result. {{8}}
The Sonnenblick bakery pays tax on its annual profit. {{9}}
